    {
      "modelVersion": "gemini-2.5-flash",
      "content": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "text": "Gracias por la observación. Tienes toda la razón, para \"episodios farmacológicos\" es mucho más apropiado utilizar la tabla `drug_era`.\n\nAquí tienes la consulta SQL corregida que utiliza la tabla `drug_era` para calcular la distribución estadística de los episodios farmacológicos por paciente:\n\n```sql\nWITH\n  DrugEraCounts AS (\n    SELECT\n      de.person_id,\n      COUNT(de.drug_era_id) AS drug_era_count\n    FROM\n      `drug_era` AS de\n    GROUP BY\n      de.person_id\n  )\nSELECT\n  AVG(drug_era_count) AS mean_drug_eras,\n  STDDEV(drug_era_count) AS stddev_drug_eras,\n  APPROX_QUANTILES(drug_era_count, 100)[OFFSET(25)] AS percentile_25_drug_eras,\n  APPROX_QUANTILES(drug_era_count, 100)[OFFSET(50)] AS percentile_50_drug_eras,\n  APPROX_QUANTILES(drug_era_count, 100)[OFFSET(75)] AS percentile_75_drug_eras\nFROM\n  DrugEraCounts\n```"
          }
        ],
